<title>RUSSIA: Fifth Russian sugar beet test has 14.3 pct sugar.</title>
<headline>Fifth Russian sugar beet test has 14.3 pct sugar.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's fifth sugar beet test had an average sugar content of 14.3 percent, against 14.0 percent in the same test in 1995, Viktor Sukhachyov, deputy head of the Rossakhsvyokla sugar beet producers' group, said on Thursday.</p>
<p>He gave the following data for the test, which was conducted on September 1 -  </p>
<p>				   5th 1996 test	 5th 1995 test</p>
<p> Avg sugar content	   14.3 pct		14.0 pct</p>
<p> Beet weight (grams)	 335		     378</p>
<p> Beets per hectare	   65,000		  68,000</p>
<p>&quot;We are still adhering to our forecast that the sugar beet harvest this year will be 17 million tonnes,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said the fifth test may have been the final one for this season, but it was possible an additional test would be conducted on September 10.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
